5. **Renal failure**: In severe cases, HbE-thalassemminemia can lead to renal failure due to iron overload from transfusion therapy.

In summary, HbE disorders are a group of hemoglobin disorders caused by a single point mutation in the β-globin chain. HbE alone is usually well tolerated, but when combined with β-thalassemia, it can lead to significant clinical consequences, including severe anemia, splenomealgia, and other complications.
