1. **Isopologues**: Isopologues are molecules that differ only in the isotopic substitution of one or more atoms, but the number of atoms and their connectivity (bonding) remain unchanged.  
2. **Isotopomers**: Isotopomers are molecules that differ only in the isotopic substitution of atoms, but the number of atoms and their connectivity (bonding) may also vary.  

Thus, allisotopomers are isotopologues, but not all isotopologues are isotopomers.  

$\boxed{\text{Isopologues are a subset of isotopomers.}}$
