   a. Butan-1-ol (CH3CH2CH2CH2OH)
   b. Butan-2-ol (CH3CH(OH)CH2CH3)

2. Functional group isomerism: This type of isomerism occurs when the same molecular formula can be represented by different functional groups. For C4H10O, the possible functional group isomers are:

   a. Butan-1-ol (CH3CH2CH2CH2OH)
   b. Butanone (CH3COCH3CH3)

In summary, the possible isomers for C4H10O are:

1. Butan-1-ol (CH3CH2CH2CH2OH)
2. Butan-2-ol (CH3CH(OH)CH2CH3)
3. Butanone (CH3COCH3CH3)

The differences between these isomers are their chemical properties and reactivity due to the different arrangements of carbon atoms and functional groups.
