","The bond between nitrogen and oxygen in the molecule NO2 (nitrogen dioxide) is polar. In NO2, nitrogen is the central atom, and there are two oxygen atoms bonded to it. The nitrogen atom has a formal charge of +1, and each oxygen atom has a formal charge of -1. This results in a polar molecule with a net dipole moment. The oxygen atoms are more electronegative than nitrogen, so they pull the electrons in the bond closer to themselves, creating a partial negative charge on the oxygen atoms and a partial positive charge on the nitrogen atom. This results in a polar bond between nitrogen and oxygen.
