E_cell = 0.4476 V - (8.314 J/mol·K * 298 K / (2 * 96485 C/mol)) * ln(0.2)
E_cell ≈ 0.4476 V - 0.0296 V = 0.418 V

Finally, we can calculate the polarization (P) as the difference between the actual cell potential and the standard cell potential:

P = E_cell - E°_cell = 0.418 V - 0.4476 V = -0.0296 V

The polarization in the electrochemical cell is -0.0296 V.
