2. **Nuclear Magnetic Resonance (NMR) Spectroscopy:** If the alcohol has a chiral center adjacent to a proton, the alcohol can be analyzed using a chiral shift shift NMR experiment. In this experiment, a chiral shift agent is added to the sample, which induces a difference in the chemical shift of the protons in the two enantiomers. This allows for the determination of the configuration of the alcohol.

