4. In conclusion, the optimal ratio of TiO2 to GO in a composite material for use in high-performance DSSCs is typically in the range of 90:10 to 70:30, with the specific ratio depending on the specific application and requirements. The addition of GO can enhance the efficiency and stability of the solar cell by improving charge carrier mobility, surface area, and stability.
