7. Nitriles: Nitriles can lose a CN group (m/z = 14) or undergo cleavage at the C-N bond, leading to the formation of a carbocation and a nitrile radical.

8. Aromatic compounds: Aromatic compounds often undergo cleavage at the C-C bond, leading to the formation of a carbocation and a radical. They can also undergo McLafferty rearrangement, which involves the migration of a hydrogen atom and a methyl group to form a neutral molecule and a carbocation.

