\]

Now, relate the molality to the mass of the unknown solute:
\[
m = \frac{\text{moles of solute}}{\text{kg of solvent}} = \frac{0.6216 \text{ g} / M_2}{0.050 \text{ kg}} = 0.1288 \text{ mol/kg}
\]

Solve for \(M_2\):
\[
M_2 = \frac{0.6216 \text{ g}}{0.1288 \text{ mol/kg} \times 0.050 \text{ kg}} = 96.55 \text{ g/mol}
