- \( L' \cdot C = P_1 + P_3 + P_6 + P_7 \),
where all seven points \( P_1, \ldots, P_7 \) are distinct. Show that \( D \) is not linearly equivalent to any other effective divisor. (Hint: Use the Residue Theorem with the conic \( LL' \).)<end_of_turn>
