","1. **Convert the speed of the train to meters per second**:  
   \( 45 \, \text{km/hr} \times \frac{1000 \, \text{m}}{1 \, \text{km}} \times \frac{1 \, \text{hr}}{60 \, \text{hr}} = 12 \, \text{m/s} \).

2. **Calculate the relative speed of the train relative to the jogger**:  
   \( 12 \, \text{m/s} - 9 \, \text{m/s} = 3 \, \text{m/s} \).  
   The train is moving 3 m/s faster than the jogger.

3. **Determine the length of the train**:  
   The train passes the jogger in 25 seconds, and its relative speed is 3 m/s.  
   The length of the train is the product of its relative speed and the time taken to pass the jogger:  
   \( 3 \, \text{m/s} \times 25 \, \text{s} = 75 \, \text{m} \).

4. **Final Answer**:  
   The length of the train is \(\boxed{75 \, \text{m}}\).
