To generate 50 sample realizations of the Wiener process, we use a random number generator to generate 50 independent sets of 11 independent standard normal variables. The recursion equation is then applied to each set of independent standard normal variables to obtain the 50 realizations. The results are arranged into a 50 × 11 matrix, where each row represents a realization.  

