\[
\Delta \lambda_{\text{max}} = \frac{2\pi \hbar}{m_e c} (1 - \cos 180^\circ) = \frac{4\pi \hbar}{m_e c}
\]  

The percentage change in wavelength is:  
\[
\text{Percentage change} = \left( \frac{\Delta \lambda_{\text{max}}}{\lambda_0} \right) \times 100\%
\]  
where \(\lambda_0 = 2.00 \, \text{Å} = 2.00 \times 10^{-10} \, \text{m}\).  

Substituting the values:  
\[
\text{Percentage change} = \left( \frac{4\pi \times 1.054 \times 10^{-34}}{9.109 \times 10^{-31} \times 3.00 \times 10^8} \right) \times \frac{1}{2.00 \times 10^{-10}} \times 100\%
